took from the discard. So my hand would have the T3 in the meld, and the T4 and T5 would be part of the meld. So after the Chi, my hand would have the meld [B7, B8, B9] and [T3, T4, T5], and the remaining tiles would be W4, W5, W7, W8, W9, F4, J3. That's 7 tiles. Wait, but 13 original tiles minus 3 (first meld) minus 3 (second meld) leaves 7. That's correct. \\n\\nNow, after forming the Chi, I can look at my remaining tiles. I have W4, W5, W7, W8, W9, F4, J3. These are 7 tiles. To form a winning hand, I need four melds and a pair. Currently, I have two melds. So I need two more melds and a pair. The remaining tiles are W4, W5, W7, W8, W9 (all in the W suit), F4 (North Wind), and J3 (White Dragon). \\n\\nLooking at the W tiles: W4, W5, W7, W8, W9. Maybe I can form a Chow of W4, W5, W6 (but W6 is not in my hand), or W7, W8, W9. I have W7, W8, W9, which is a valid Chow. So if I have those, that's another meld. Then I would have three melds, and need one more meld and a pair. The remaining tiles would be W4, W5, F4, J3. \\n\\nWait, if I form a Chow of W7, W8, W9, that uses three tiles. Then the remaining tiles are W4, W5, F4, J3. That's four tiles. To form a fourth meld and a pair, I need to have either another Chow or a Pung or Kong. But W4 and W5 can't form a Chow without W3 or W6. So maybe I can form a pair with F4 and J3. But F4 is North Wind, which is my seat wind. Since my seat wind is North, having a Pung or Kong of North Wind would give me 2 points (Seat Wind). But I only have one F4. So that's not possible. \\n\\nAlternatively, maybe I can form a pair of W4 and W5. But they are different numbers. So no. \\n\\nSo after forming the two Chows (B7-B8-B9 and T3-T4-T5), and another Chow of W7-W8-W9, I would have three melds and need one more. The remaining tiles would be W4, W5, F4, J3. These don't form a meld. So I need to see if there's another way. \\n\\nAlternatively, maybe I can form a Pung with F4 or J3, but I only have one of each. So that's not possible. \\n\