, the best move is to play W5.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: Playing W5 allows forming a potential chow in the W suit if W3 or W6 is drawn, completing four chows and a pair for the All Chows pattern (2 points). This is more efficient than waiting for a pair of T9s, as the chow would directly contribute to a higher-scoring structure.\n\nReason: Forming a fourth chow with W3/W4/W5 or W4/W5/W6 would complete four chows and a pair, fulfilling the All Chows pattern (2 points) while maintaining flexibility. Playing W5 maximizes the chance to complete this structure, as W3 and W6 are still available (3 copies each). A T9 pair would only add a pair without enhancing the existing meld structure.\n\nAnswer: Play W5"}
